  "hm.h": "Kid home screen", "sd.home": "KidGuard replaces the home screen: only apps your kid may use show up", "hm.on": "Turn on the KidGuard home screen", "hm.style": "Starting style", "hm.sAuto": "Default (Teen)", "hm.sBe": "Kid (6–10)", "hm.sTeen": "Teen", "hm.sGon": "Compact", "hm.settings": "Let your kid open Settings (the Settings app, long-press in the control center opens settings pages). Off: the Settings icon is hidden and long-press is locked. Your kid can still turn Wi-Fi / Bluetooth / data on, just not off. Some phones still reach Settings from a system panel (e.g. Wi-Fi)", "hm.notes": "Show your note when an app is paused", "hm.lock": "Lock Customize (your kid can still arrange apps)", "hm.shade": "Block the phone's quick settings (Wi-Fi, airplane, data…)", "hm.shadeHint": "Notifications work as usual. Pulling on to quick settings closes them, and the kid uses KidGuard's own control center. The small button row above the notifications still works. Needs KidGuard's Accessibility; not on the lock screen.", "hm.kidNotes": "Notes your kid shared", "hm.tip": "Blocked apps and new apps waiting for approval don't show; apps out of time are greyed, and tapping one shows why plus a More time button. Phone is always the first dock slot (hold it for 112–115). Turning it off brings the phone's own home screen back. The style only applies the first time; your kid can change it later.", "hm.stOn": "Running on the kid's phone", "hm.stWait": "Waiting for the kid's phone…", "hm.stCrash": "Turned itself off for 24 h after repeated crashes", "hm.stHome": "Home opens another app", "hm.stNoOwner": "Needs Device Owner", "hm.stOld": "The kid's phone needs a newer KidGuard",
  "frp.h": "Lock the phone to your Google account after a factory reset",
  "frp.ph": "Google account ID (digits), e.g. 112233445566778899001",
  "frp.how": "How to get the ID",
  "frp.tip": "Needs the numeric Google account ID, not the email. Easiest way: open developers.google.com/oauthplayground, sign in with the parent's Google account, authorize the scope \"profile\", then call GET https://people.googleapis.com/v1/people/me?personFields=metadata and copy the number after \"people/\". Up to 5 IDs, separated by spaces. Careful: after a reset the phone only unlocks with one of these accounts. A wrong ID can lock the phone for good.",
  "frp.unsup": "Needs Device Owner and Android 11 or newer.",
  "frp.err": "The phone refused the setting.",
