  "sup.h": "Report a problem to the developer",
  "sup.intro": "The child's phone sends its technical status to the KidGuard developer and gets an 8-digit code. The developer's replies show here (the phone asks every 6 hours). Reports are kept 14 days.",
  "sup.whatH": "What is sent?",
  "sup.what": "Sent: version, phone make and model, Android, mode (Device Owner / basic), permissions and features on, the names of the rules that are on (no apps, times or places), relay / Tailscale / Telegram status, battery, KidGuard's technical log and its last crash. Before sending, the phone removes keys, tokens, emails, MAC addresses, Wi-Fi names, coordinates, public IPs, any non-English words and app names.",
  "sup.never": "Never sent: location and track, notifications, the child's notes, photos, files, the app list and screen time. One app's name goes only if you pick it below.",
  "sup.kind": "Problem with",
